WEBVTT

00:01.002 --> 00:04.816
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.817 --> 00:08.174
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.175 --> 00:11.744
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.745 --> 00:14.747
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.748 --> 00:18.250
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.251 --> 00:21.420
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.421 --> 00:23.191
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.192 --> 00:24.423
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.424 --> 00:30.151
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy.</i>

00:37.573 --> 00:39.229
So what's the big emergency?

00:39.230 --> 00:41.255
Why did everyone
have to come in on a Monday?

00:41.256 --> 00:43.745
I'm afraid we have troubling news.

00:43.746 --> 00:46.814
Due to budget cuts, we'll
be laying off one employee.

00:49.151 --> 00:51.519
The Internet pretty much
only lets us fire white males,

00:51.520 --> 00:54.989
so if you're not
a white male, you're safe.

00:54.990 --> 00:56.858
- So, is Derek Jeter safe?
- Safe!

00:56.859 --> 00:58.526
- What?
- He's half black.

00:58.527 --> 00:59.927
- What? What do you need, glasses?
- No, I don't need glasses.

00:59.928 --> 01:01.341
He's white by a mile. He tucks...

01:01.343 --> 01:03.031
You're the one who needs glasses.

01:03.032 --> 01:04.832
And what happened to this kind
of coach-umpire confrontation?

01:04.833 --> 01:06.701
- I know, I miss it, too.
- It used to happen a lot in the '70s

01:06.702 --> 01:08.770
but doesn't seem to happen
that much anymore.

01:08.771 --> 01:11.368
to a bygone era when
men settled their differences

01:11.369 --> 01:12.940
I agree. That's what we're doing now.

01:12.941 --> 01:14.477
Thrusting their chests into one another.

01:14.478 --> 01:16.433
I miss having a guy yell in my mouth.

01:16.434 --> 01:18.489
And while we're talking about stuff,
I've never cleaned my ice trays.

01:18.490 --> 01:20.228
- Oh, you have to do that.
- Why do I have to?

01:20.229 --> 01:22.129
- You're poisoning your family.
- It's just water and water.

01:22.130 --> 01:25.153
Carrying an ice tray from
the freezer to the sink is like ringing

01:25.154 --> 01:27.214
- the damn dinner bell for arm hairs.
- Come to think of it,

01:27.215 --> 01:29.149
but I don't remember seeing a few
short hairs in my ice cubes

01:29.150 --> 01:30.754
Of course they're getting in there.

01:30.755 --> 01:33.227
- That I'm hoping were from my arm.
- Clean your trays.

01:33.228 --> 01:35.963
Oh, cool off, Griffin.
It is no big deal.

01:35.964 --> 01:37.532
It's just that someone's getting fired

01:37.533 --> 01:40.234
- in front of everybody tomorrow.
- Well, that sounds fine.

01:40.235 --> 01:42.537
I guess I'll just see you... What?!

01:42.538 --> 01:44.072
Old joke. You're out.

01:44.073 --> 01:46.741
- Old joke? I put my own twist on it.
- There was no twist.

01:46.742 --> 01:49.377
Oh, you're crazy.
It was a tip of the hat to my son.

01:49.378 --> 01:51.779
If anything,
it's a gift to our long-time viewers.

01:51.780 --> 01:53.748
Merry Christmas.
Here's a warmed-over turd

01:53.749 --> 01:55.822
from ten years ago.

01:58.821 --> 02:00.885
Okay, I can do this.

02:00.886 --> 02:03.691
No need to be nervous.
Just show 'em that I'm good at my job.

02:03.692 --> 02:05.359
That's it. Easy peasy.

02:05.360 --> 02:07.361
Hey there, PG.

02:07.362 --> 02:08.730
Been a minute.

02:08.731 --> 02:11.199
Hey, Ernie. I mean, I mean
Cookie Monst... I mean Bert.

02:11.200 --> 02:12.233
Bert. Sorry.

02:12.234 --> 02:13.735
Oh, it's okay, Peter.

02:13.736 --> 02:15.236
Just do what you would normally do.

02:15.237 --> 02:16.871
Pretend I'm not here.

02:16.872 --> 02:18.573
Oh, pretend you're not here? All right.

02:18.574 --> 02:21.041
God, that Bert is an idiot.

02:21.042 --> 02:22.522
What a pud.

02:22.523 --> 02:23.711
But I wouldn't mind
getting to know that Sheila

02:23.712 --> 02:24.879
a little better.

02:24.880 --> 02:26.447
She's got a great dumper.

02:26.448 --> 02:28.950
And by dumper,
I mean fecal thoroughfare.

02:28.951 --> 02:30.785
Should I...?

02:30.786 --> 02:32.120
Yeah, answer it.

02:32.121 --> 02:35.156
Could be important for the company.

02:37.493 --> 02:38.960
Goodbye?

02:38.961 --> 02:40.962
Ah, shoot. Opposite of that, yeah?

02:40.963 --> 02:42.663
Let's roll to the break room, Peter.

02:42.664 --> 02:44.665
We're ready to announce
who's getting fired.

02:44.666 --> 02:46.968
Oh, sure, if Sheila and her
wastemaker are gonna be there.

02:46.969 --> 02:50.122
Please stop talking about
my wife's anal processes.

02:57.646 --> 03:01.415
Opie, will you accept this stein?

03:07.923 --> 03:10.258
Bachelor Nick? Why are you here?

03:10.259 --> 03:12.426
They make me come to all these things.

03:12.427 --> 03:14.170
Cool. How's Vanessa?

03:14.171 --> 03:15.963
- We broke up.
- Aw.

03:15.964 --> 03:18.800
I would murder my family
for one hour with Corinne.

03:18.801 --> 03:21.075
Eh, she was a little young.

03:22.171 --> 03:24.105
You know how stupid you sound?

03:24.106 --> 03:26.816
Peter, take a step forward.

03:27.943 --> 03:30.378
I-I'm sorry. I-I keep messing up.

03:30.379 --> 03:33.792
You're seeing me at my worst.
I'm very nervous.

03:40.422 --> 03:42.423
My life is flashing before my eyes.

03:42.424 --> 03:46.160
And for some reason, it's all
just the sort of gay moments.

04:01.042 --> 04:02.958
Excuse me, is someone sitting here?

04:02.959 --> 04:04.879
Yes. My lover, Tom.

04:06.315 --> 04:09.550
Oh, Peter! I'm so happy you're okay.

04:09.551 --> 04:11.839
Whoa, you're alive?

04:11.840 --> 04:14.021
What happened?
Did I have a heart attack?

04:14.022 --> 04:15.656
No, you had a panic attack.

04:15.657 --> 04:18.426
Or, in medical terms,
"a heart attack for wussies."

04:18.427 --> 04:19.727
Hey, we have a bet going.

04:19.728 --> 04:21.729
Do you remember if you put
your wrist to your forehead

04:21.730 --> 04:23.564
like a nancy-boy when you fainted?

04:23.565 --> 04:25.466
I choose not to answer.

04:25.467 --> 04:28.002
Peter, you need to get
your stress under control.

04:28.003 --> 04:30.071
I'm texting you a link
to a collection of songs

04:30.072 --> 04:31.505
called yacht rock.

04:31.506 --> 04:32.740
Any time I'm feeling stressed,

04:32.741 --> 04:35.109
I play this music,
and it really mellows me out.

04:35.110 --> 04:37.612
- I think it'll work for you.
- Well, what is that? Is that like...

04:37.613 --> 04:40.047
<i>Da, da, da, da, da, da, da, da.</i>

04:40.048 --> 04:41.315
No, no, it's more like...

04:41.316 --> 04:42.650
<i>Ia, da, da, da, da</i>

04:42.651 --> 04:43.951
<i>Da, da, da, da, da.</i>

04:43.952 --> 04:46.687
<i>Oh, good. It's... Ia, da, da, da, da</i>

04:46.688 --> 04:48.522
<i>Da, da, da, da.
'Cause I don't like that.</i>

04:48.523 --> 04:50.458
<i>Da, da, da, ba, ba, ba.</i>

04:50.459 --> 04:52.793
<i>No, I assure you, it's... Ia, da, da, da</i>

04:52.794 --> 04:54.395
<i>Da, da, da, da, da, da, da.</i>

04:54.396 --> 04:55.830
Now, if you'll excuse me,

04:55.831 --> 04:58.966
I have more music
to prescribe to sick patients.

05:02.504 --> 05:04.939
- So, Peter, you feeling better?
- Yeah, I guess.

05:04.940 --> 05:07.408
The doctor just said
I'm too stressed out.

05:07.409 --> 05:09.777
Did the doctor give you anything
to help, you know,

05:09.778 --> 05:11.379
mellow you out?

05:11.380 --> 05:13.648
<i>ВїLos drogas?</i>

05:13.649 --> 05:16.884
No, he just gave me this link
for something called yacht rock.

05:18.854 --> 05:20.788
This one's called "Summer Breeze,"

05:20.789 --> 05:23.958
and it makes me feel fine.

05:23.959 --> 05:26.093
This music... I...

05:26.094 --> 05:28.829
I feel like I'm dirty dancing
with a sunset.

05:32.134 --> 05:34.302
Uh, guys, there's a yacht rock cruise

05:34.303 --> 05:37.171
that leaves
from the Quahog Marina tomorrow.

05:37.172 --> 05:39.707
And I'm not even kidding.

05:39.708 --> 05:42.343
You know what, guys? We haven't
gone anywhere in a long time.

05:42.344 --> 05:43.811
So, let's do it.

05:43.812 --> 05:45.413
Cleveland, buy those tickets,

05:45.414 --> 05:47.648
'cause the guys are going
on a yacht rock cruise.

05:47.649 --> 05:49.150
- Yeah!
- Awesome!

05:49.151 --> 05:51.406
Peter? Is that you?

05:51.407 --> 05:53.487
- Do I know you?
- I-It's me. Lyle?

05:53.488 --> 05:55.189
From the other side of the aquarium?

05:55.190 --> 05:57.024
I-I... I don't... I don't know you.

05:57.025 --> 05:59.360
I-I don't... I don't know
what you're talking about.

05:59.361 --> 06:01.662
<i>But I did know
what he was talking about.</i>

06:01.663 --> 06:03.831
<i>I spent the next two and a half years</i>

06:03.832 --> 06:06.154
<i>cruising various aquariums.</i>

06:06.155 --> 06:07.969
<i>I never did find Lyle.</i>

06:07.970 --> 06:11.172
<i>Also, I didn't quite clear the table.</i>

06:22.965 --> 06:25.833
I got to say, Peter, I had
reservations about this cruise,

06:25.834 --> 06:27.668
but you do seem more relaxed.

06:27.669 --> 06:29.236
Hey, good thing I had reservations

06:29.237 --> 06:30.938
<i>on this cruise, huh?</i>

06:30.939 --> 06:33.190
I don't mind dad jokes.

06:33.191 --> 06:34.731
Everyone's included.

06:37.112 --> 06:38.646
Looks like mine won't be the only tail

06:38.647 --> 06:40.381
I'll be chasing this week.

06:40.382 --> 06:43.751
- Hey. What the...
- All dogs have to be crated below deck.

06:45.921 --> 06:47.488
Stewie, help!

06:47.489 --> 06:49.190
I knew this was a possibility, so I put

06:49.191 --> 06:53.027
a 1982 Mattel Electronic
Baseball game in your bag.

06:54.596 --> 06:56.097
Okay, that's something.

06:56.098 --> 06:58.099
The battery might be
a little old, though.

07:07.342 --> 07:08.843
Peter, you brought your family?

07:08.844 --> 07:11.145
This was supposed to be a guys' trip.

07:11.146 --> 07:12.672
Please don't tell Donna.
- Please don't tell Bonnie.

07:12.673 --> 07:14.682
- She hasn't been on a vacation...
- She'll kill me if...

07:14.683 --> 07:16.050
- Please, Lois, please.
- Please, Lois.

07:16.051 --> 07:17.485
- Promise me. Here, look,
- Promise me first.

07:17.486 --> 07:19.020
- I'm putting money
- Here's my gun. Do you want it?

07:19.021 --> 07:20.921
- In your purse.
- I-I'm sorry, I couldn't hear you.

07:20.922 --> 07:23.057
I'm sending a selfie
to Bonnie and Donna.

07:23.058 --> 07:24.892
Cruise, bitches.

07:24.893 --> 07:27.228
- Don't hit send, please don't hit send.
- Please don't hit send.

07:27.229 --> 07:29.296
And... send.

07:30.766 --> 07:33.901
You son of a bitch.

07:33.902 --> 07:35.903
- I told you.
- What did he do now?

07:35.904 --> 07:37.571
He don't listen to you.

07:37.572 --> 07:40.541
He don't listen to you.

07:42.277 --> 07:43.611
What is it, Bonnie?

07:43.612 --> 07:46.280
Nothing, Father Monaghan.

07:46.281 --> 07:48.582
- Well, this sucks now.
- Our whole trip's ruined,

07:48.583 --> 07:50.084
thanks to you, Peter.

07:50.085 --> 07:52.219
Thank God Bonnie's got Father Monaghan

07:52.220 --> 07:54.255
for spiritual counsel.

07:54.256 --> 07:55.690
Well, it's not my fault
you guys are too stupid

07:55.691 --> 07:57.124
to understand what the plan was.

07:57.125 --> 07:59.671
The plan was clear.
You're the stupid one.

07:59.672 --> 08:03.197
What?

08:03.198 --> 08:06.667
<i>Sailing takes me away...</i>

08:06.668 --> 08:09.303
- What were we fighting about?
- I don't know.

08:09.304 --> 08:12.273
My cares have all suddenly melted away.

08:12.274 --> 08:15.376
Are my toes tapping?
I feel like my toes are tapping.

08:15.377 --> 08:17.645
Nah, there's a seagull
pecking at your foot.

08:18.980 --> 08:20.514
Whenever I wear my Tevas,

08:20.515 --> 08:23.295
my toes are up for grabs.

08:25.020 --> 08:27.054
Hey, Cleveland, this is us.

08:27.055 --> 08:28.656
You guys got to stop by later.

08:28.657 --> 08:31.392
Snuck on a little of this action.

08:31.393 --> 08:33.609
What? You guys are sharing a room?

08:33.610 --> 08:36.430
- You're adults.
- I'm not paying full price for a room.

08:36.431 --> 08:38.566
Have some self-respect. You're 40.

08:38.567 --> 08:40.568
It's not like
we're gonna be in there much.

08:40.569 --> 08:42.744
Too busy scoping trim.

08:42.745 --> 08:45.703
I may bail to the room to catch a nap.

08:45.704 --> 08:47.771
Right behind you, roomie.

08:47.772 --> 08:50.845
After we wake,
we gonna fire up that Keurig.

08:50.846 --> 08:54.482
Oh, yeah, that's why I brought
along a couple of these babies.

08:55.650 --> 08:58.252
Wait, there's only one bed.

08:58.253 --> 09:00.354
I know. We're going head to toe.

09:00.355 --> 09:02.757
Say hello to your pillow.

09:02.758 --> 09:05.426
Hi there, do you know if singer
and songwriter Bob Welch

09:05.427 --> 09:06.761
is on board yet?

09:06.762 --> 09:09.930
He's not, because he died in 2012.

09:11.833 --> 09:13.781
Can you give me a moment?

09:14.336 --> 09:17.171
<i>Sentimental gentle wind</i>

09:17.172 --> 09:20.341
<i>Blowing through my life again...</i>

09:20.342 --> 09:23.844
I can't believe Bob Welch
is really gone.

09:23.845 --> 09:25.813
<i>Gentle one...</i>

09:25.814 --> 09:29.850
Hey... we just heard about Bob Welch.

09:29.851 --> 09:31.852
<i>Blowing through my life again...</i>

09:31.853 --> 09:33.521
Yeah.

09:33.522 --> 09:35.756
Who the (BLEEP) is Bob Welch?

09:45.041 --> 09:47.268
Okay, for the first game,
I choose Alan Parsons

09:47.269 --> 09:49.603
as my teammate, but not The Project.

09:49.604 --> 09:51.272
I want nothing to do with them.

09:51.273 --> 09:53.007
We'll play Joe and Loggins.

09:53.008 --> 09:55.276
- Thanks for picking me, Peter.
- No problem.

09:55.277 --> 09:57.611
"Crosby, Stills, Nash"
to see who goes first?

09:57.612 --> 09:59.814
Crosby, Stills, Nash, shoot.

09:59.815 --> 10:02.883
- Nash. I win.
- No, Crosby eats Nash.

10:02.884 --> 10:05.853
- Stills snorts Crosby.
- What does Nash do?

10:05.854 --> 10:07.855
Nash smokes Stills.

10:07.856 --> 10:10.706
So, Kenny, "Footloose."

10:10.707 --> 10:12.893
Not really a song for everyone.

10:12.894 --> 10:16.599
<i>Well, maybe you'd prefer my song
in Caddyshack, "I'm Alright."</i>

10:16.600 --> 10:20.127
Wh-What, do you think I'm stupid
because I'm in a chair?

10:20.128 --> 10:21.762
I'll pull the tape, guy.

10:21.763 --> 10:24.238
The gopher sang that song.

10:29.087 --> 10:31.378
This is so exciting.
What do you want to do tonight?

10:31.379 --> 10:33.814
What if we just go see a movie?

10:33.815 --> 10:36.250
We can see a movie at home.
We need to go out.

10:36.251 --> 10:37.651
Shake things up.

10:37.652 --> 10:40.054
We're here to experience
new things, be other people.

10:40.055 --> 10:42.256
Mm-hmm.

10:42.257 --> 10:44.258
How much wine have you had tonight?

10:45.760 --> 10:47.761
Maybe we could hang out
with that nice couple

10:47.762 --> 10:50.030
- we met the other day.
- The Federmans?

10:50.031 --> 10:52.266
Why do you always want
to hang out with other people

10:52.267 --> 10:53.934
when we're on vacation?

10:53.935 --> 10:55.669
It's just nice to meet new people.

10:55.670 --> 10:59.406
Right, because I'm so interested
in the medical supply business.

10:59.407 --> 11:01.442
- Why do you always do that?
- Do what?

11:01.443 --> 11:03.444
Diminish people.

11:03.445 --> 11:04.879
Oh, that's why.

11:04.880 --> 11:07.982
Well, I feel like this has
become a referendum on me,

11:07.983 --> 11:11.002
and I don't appreciate it.

11:12.087 --> 11:14.221
Did you pack my dandruff shampoo?

11:14.222 --> 11:15.689
No.

11:15.690 --> 11:18.425
Then I guess this black shirt is out.

11:18.426 --> 11:20.794
You just want to hang out
with Doug Federman.

11:20.795 --> 11:23.397
What? That's... that's the wine talking.

11:23.398 --> 11:25.599
What does Doug Federman have
that I don't?

11:25.600 --> 11:27.268
A job.

11:27.269 --> 11:30.437
I'm going to watch the magic
show in the Cognac Club.

11:30.438 --> 11:32.172
Why, because there's
a two-drink minimum?

11:32.173 --> 11:34.975
Oh, you shut up!

11:34.976 --> 11:36.310
Thank you.

11:36.311 --> 11:38.779
For my next trick,
I'll need a volunteer.

11:38.780 --> 11:41.148
- How about you, sir?
- No, I don't want to!

11:41.149 --> 11:43.659
I don't want to do it.

11:46.521 --> 11:49.356
Bell, Biv, DeVoe, shoot.

11:49.357 --> 11:51.392
- Gotcha.
- What do you mean?

11:51.393 --> 11:53.627
I win. Bell bivs DeVoe.

11:53.628 --> 11:56.230
Dude, you can't "biv" someone.
Biv's a guy.

11:56.231 --> 11:59.600
Everybody on this cruise is boring.

12:01.763 --> 12:05.639
I can show you where there's
a whole pile of those.

12:06.853 --> 12:08.025
Cigarette butts?

12:08.026 --> 12:10.477
Yeah. The wind blows them all
to this one spot.

12:10.478 --> 12:12.346
It's right by where the seagulls crap.

12:12.347 --> 12:15.516
It's my job to clean it up.
That's how I know about it.

12:15.517 --> 12:18.018
You must know a lot about crap.

12:18.019 --> 12:19.687
You're not from here, are you?

12:19.688 --> 12:22.089
From the cruise? No. I'm from a town.

12:22.090 --> 12:24.024
You want to mess around
on some damp towels

12:24.025 --> 12:25.426
next to where the seagulls crap?

12:25.427 --> 12:26.860
It wasn't seagulls.

12:26.861 --> 12:28.696
I got locked out of my room earlier.

12:28.697 --> 12:30.030
Oh.

12:30.031 --> 12:32.433
- Why is your poop white?
- I don't know.

12:32.434 --> 12:35.936
I've been dealing with
fecal albinism my whole life.

12:35.937 --> 12:38.973
<i>All I want to do
in the middle of the evening</i>

12:38.974 --> 12:41.375
<i>Is hold you tight</i>

12:41.376 --> 12:45.045
<i>Rosanna, Rosanna</i>

12:45.046 --> 12:47.448
<i>I didn't know you were
looking for more than</i>

12:47.449 --> 12:49.216
<i>I could ever be...</i>

12:49.217 --> 12:50.651
Hey, what are you guys up to?

12:50.652 --> 12:53.554
We're making a food spread in room 103.

12:53.555 --> 12:54.655
Come on by.

12:54.656 --> 12:57.124
Grab some cocktail sauce on your way.

12:57.125 --> 13:00.294
Oh, wait. Never mind.

13:00.295 --> 13:01.962
Aah! Damn it.

13:01.963 --> 13:05.632
<i>We're watching Michael Clayton
on DVD later. Be there.</i>

13:08.937 --> 13:12.473
By the way, I, uh,
heard about Bob Welch.

13:12.474 --> 13:14.208
I'm sorry.

13:14.209 --> 13:16.610
Don't know what else to say.

13:16.611 --> 13:19.513
- Sending good vibes.
- Yeah...

13:19.514 --> 13:21.115
Can you give me a moment?

13:21.116 --> 13:24.151
<i>Sentimental gentle wind</i>

13:24.152 --> 13:27.421
<i>Blowing through my life again</i>

13:27.422 --> 13:29.256
<i>Sentimental Lady...</i>

13:29.257 --> 13:31.892
- Bob Welch?
- Bob Welch.

13:31.893 --> 13:34.128
- Hey, aren't you the captain?
- Yes.

13:34.129 --> 13:37.106
Well, if you're here,
who's driving the boat?

13:38.033 --> 13:40.167
Oh, my God!

13:44.418 --> 13:47.274
Wow, I've never seen someone
eat so many powdered Donettes

13:47.275 --> 13:48.609
in half an hour before.

13:48.610 --> 13:49.843
Yeah, I was really hungry,

13:49.844 --> 13:51.712
and I didn't like
what they had at dinner.

13:51.713 --> 13:55.064
I think we may have solved
your fecal albinism.

13:55.065 --> 13:56.817
I love you, Meg.

13:56.818 --> 13:58.819
Oh, my God,

13:58.820 --> 14:01.021
no one's ever told me that before.

14:01.022 --> 14:03.190
This is the best night of my li...

14:28.683 --> 14:31.185
Listen to all those idiots fall.

14:31.186 --> 14:33.821
- Honey, don't revel in it.
- Hey, I need this.

14:33.822 --> 14:35.989
I just found out Bob Welch died.

14:35.990 --> 14:38.592
<i>Sentimental gentle wind</i>

14:38.593 --> 14:40.194
<i>Blowing...</i>

14:40.195 --> 14:42.763
- Aah! What are we gonna do?
- I don't know.

14:42.764 --> 14:46.300
And, look, Oates is hanging on
to Hall for dear life.

14:47.902 --> 14:50.504
What else is new? He's been
doing that for 40 years.

14:50.505 --> 14:53.674
Ha, ha. Yeah, make fun of more people

14:53.675 --> 14:55.776
more successful than you.

14:55.777 --> 14:57.344
He's a millionaire.

14:57.345 --> 14:59.379
You're nothing.

15:15.654 --> 15:17.889
Oh, thank God we're all okay.

15:17.890 --> 15:19.991
Looks like Oates wasn't so lucky.

15:28.400 --> 15:30.668
Guys, it's me, Kenny Loggins.

15:30.669 --> 15:32.169
First of all, I'm all right.

15:32.170 --> 15:33.571
Don't nobody worry about me.

15:33.572 --> 15:35.006
Gopher!

15:35.007 --> 15:37.775
This boat has flipped over.
We need to get up to the hull.

15:37.776 --> 15:39.243
There's a spot in the propeller room

15:39.244 --> 15:41.078
where the hull's only an inch thick.

15:41.079 --> 15:43.047
Maybe we can try to cut our way out...

15:47.452 --> 15:50.454
Hey, you sons of bitches!

15:51.790 --> 15:53.090
This is Chad!

15:53.091 --> 15:55.426
He's my boyfriend. We love each other.

15:55.427 --> 15:58.162
We said it and everything.

16:02.334 --> 16:03.792
A little help?

16:41.540 --> 16:42.707
Hi-yah!

16:57.850 --> 16:59.824
Preesh.

17:14.673 --> 17:16.841
Guys, we got to get out of here.

17:33.658 --> 17:35.960
- You're alive.
- And well.

17:35.961 --> 17:38.629
We got to get out of here. The
water levels are rising fast.

17:38.630 --> 17:40.431
I'll just grab an apple real quick.

17:40.432 --> 17:43.200
Granny Smith? What,
do you got a oven in your mouth?

17:43.201 --> 17:46.670
- Huh?
- Pie apple. It's a pie apple.

17:46.671 --> 17:48.539
I like a good Red Delicious.

17:48.540 --> 17:50.408
Oh, does your mouth have a lid on it?

17:50.409 --> 17:51.776
What are you talking about?

17:51.777 --> 17:54.712
That's a garbage apple.
May as well eat a Honeycrisp.

17:54.713 --> 17:57.314
- What's wrong with that one?
- Science apple.

17:57.315 --> 18:00.117
Made in a lab
with test tubes and beakers.

18:00.118 --> 18:02.553
<i>Well, what apples do you like?</i>

18:02.554 --> 18:04.955
Fuji for eating, crab for huckin'.

18:04.956 --> 18:06.791
That's a prankster's apple.

18:06.792 --> 18:09.527
Gosh, Cleveland, I had no idea
you knew so much about apples.

18:09.528 --> 18:12.663
- Hmm. Did you ever ask?
- No, I guess I didn't.

18:12.664 --> 18:14.165
Hmm.

18:22.774 --> 18:26.077
I can't open it!

18:26.078 --> 18:28.546
There's too much water
pushing from the other side!

18:28.547 --> 18:30.014
So we're stuck?

18:30.015 --> 18:32.583
Yeah, unless we can
somehow tip the boat.

18:32.584 --> 18:34.585
<i>Maybe we can.</i>

18:34.586 --> 18:36.487
What are you talking about,
Michael McDonald?

18:36.488 --> 18:38.222
<i>The timbre in my voice</i>

18:38.223 --> 18:40.491
<i>Allows me to communicate with whales.</i>

18:40.492 --> 18:42.460
<i>Maybe they can help.</i>

19:26.638 --> 19:28.472
Oh, we... oh, we found him.

19:28.473 --> 19:31.075
(BLEEP)! You guys left me
down there to drown.

19:31.076 --> 19:33.511
Technically, we left you
up there to drown.

19:33.512 --> 19:36.180
- The boat flipped.
- You know what you did.

19:36.181 --> 19:38.249
I think the only way
to teach you a lesson

19:38.250 --> 19:40.551
is to dog-shake and get you all wet.

19:40.552 --> 19:41.986
- No, Brian, don't!
- I'm doing it.

19:44.656 --> 19:45.923
All right, we're even.

19:48.944 --> 19:50.628
Well, we found the thinnest part
of the hull,

19:50.629 --> 19:52.363
but it's still an inch thick.

19:52.364 --> 19:56.000
Yeah, of steel. How are we
supposed to get through that?

20:11.789 --> 20:14.791
Man, that was crazy.

20:16.782 --> 20:18.135
I'm Casey Kasem.

20:18.136 --> 20:20.050
Coming in at number seven
on the countdown,

20:20.051 --> 20:22.720
that was Peter Griffin
with "Yacht Rocky,"

20:22.721 --> 20:24.310
down three spots.

20:24.311 --> 20:25.823
Now for our number six.

20:25.824 --> 20:27.425
<i>Number six.</i>

20:27.426 --> 20:30.526
We'll start with a letter
from Melanie in Kansas.

20:30.527 --> 20:32.767
She writes, "Dear Casey,

20:32.768 --> 20:35.599
"is Christopher Cross
as nice as he seems?

20:35.600 --> 20:37.859
"Also, aren't you dead?

20:37.860 --> 20:39.403
"And why did your large wife

20:39.404 --> 20:41.814
"hide your body from your children?"

20:41.815 --> 20:45.276
Well, the answer to your first
question is a resounding yes.

20:45.277 --> 20:48.086
Christopher Cross
is a perfect gentleman.

20:48.087 --> 20:49.793
And as for the second question,

20:49.794 --> 20:51.059
you're correct, Melanie.

20:51.060 --> 20:52.465
I'm extremely dead,

20:52.466 --> 20:55.204
and I do wish my children
could have closure.

20:55.205 --> 20:57.650
Honey, if you're listening, please,

20:57.651 --> 21:00.107
just put my body in the ground.

21:00.108 --> 21:02.472
And now back to the countdown.

21:02.473 --> 22:03.473
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv